  *
  * When stderr is not a tty (pipe, CI log, file) every function is a no-op, so
  * output stays byte-identical to upstream fastboot.
+ *
+ * SailTool patch: setting FORCE_PROGRESS=1 overrides only the tty requirement,
+ * so a caller reading stderr through a pipe still gets the bar as plain,
+ * \r-separated text (colours stay off — they have their own detection).
+ * NO_PROGRESS=1 still wins over it.
  */
